### 4.4 Jump Statements

```
break_statement  = 'break'
skip_statement   = 'skip' [ expression ]
return_statement = 'return' [ expression ]
                 | 'give back' [ expression ]
```

`break` and `skip` act on the innermost loop the statement is written inside, and
end the block they were written in as well as the loop — a `catch`, `finally`,
`test` or `object` body inside a loop is inside that loop. With no enclosing loop
they are a runtime error, `'<keyword>' is only valid inside a loop`, which
`try ... catch error` catches; a function body is not inside the loop that called
it, so a `break` in one is refused too. See SPEC.md, "Break and Skip".
